      "id": "integration",
      "name": "Integration",
      "description": "It does not choose its own places; it grows out of the ones the horse already has. Anywhere the coat is dark - the crest and the base of the mane, a dorsal stripe, the distal limbs, the margin of any other marking - becomes a source, and elements propagate outward from it. Right at a source they merge into continuous patches with scalloped margins; a hand's span out they are separate circles and lobes with their long axis pointing the way they came; further still they thin to nothing. It reads as an appaloosa blanket at medium scale.",
